Chapter: EffectDottedAllow
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Lattice probe, right direction (effect rows stage 0). A callee
 declares the sub-effect [Console.Write] (over-declared; its body is
 pure, which is always allowed). A caller declared [Console] calls
 it: Console.Write is covered by Console via the dotted prefix
 relation (effect-covered-by). Must compile today and under rows.
 Regression-tests CL 6509: find-dot must find the CCE dot, not
 ASCII 46, or the prefix relation is dead code and this rejects.

Section: Definitions

  narrow : Integer -> [Console.Write] Integer
  narrow (n) = n + 1

  caller : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  caller (n) = narrow n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (caller 41))
  end
